{
 "_doc": [
  "Evidence behind docs/RESULTS.md 2026-08-19 'The gate was the bug' and",
  "'The one rotation nothing can contradict'. Two independent measurements.",
  "",
  "orientation_osd: for every testset frame, Tesseract OSD's rotate call and",
  "  confidence on the raw (mirror-baked) buffer, and the same on that buffer",
  "  deliberately rotated 180. The second arm is the POSITIVE population for a",
  "  180 call - the only way to see what a CORRECT 180 scores, since no fixture",
  "  is naturally upside down. It also refutes flip-and-compare: on 6 of the 7",
  "  wrong calls OSD repeats its wrong answer on the flipped buffer.",
  "",
  "stitch_sweep: every (close-up, variant) attempt on the 4 real zoomset sets.",
  "  'ncc' is photometric agreement after warping - the correctness signal that",
  "  does NOT come from the matcher, so it can referee a change to the matcher.",
  "  Verified by eye on full-resolution checkerboard overlays: ncc >= 0.45 lines",
  "  up, ncc <= 0.28 does not.",
  "",
  "stitch_ocr: OCR of every frame standalone, and of the Stage 01 anchor before",
  "  vs after blending. NO GROUND TRUTH exists for the zoomset, so word counts",
  "  and confidences are INDICATIVE, not accuracy."
 ],
